I can only compare this to how I do it in mgcv, gam, and INLA. In INLA I'm using the posterior means of the prediction stack and not the estimation stack to compute the P value. Using gam and mgcv we do 1000 permutations of predicting the model and then comparing it by ANOVA to an aspatial model, and the P value in this case signifies where the spatial model is superior to the aspatial model. So in those cases at least the P value is based on prediction.

BTW I'm using brms 1.8.0

