From u6a81821136f21d6b at groups.google.com  Thu Aug 17 20:43:16 2017
From: u6a81821136f21d6b at groups.google.com (steven....@gmail.com)
Date: Thu, 17 Aug 2017 20:43:16 +0000
Subject: Multiple models in one compilation
Message-ID: <Pxl3QR5C1e0.DJor4IspEQAJ@brms-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/brms-users/c/Pxl3QR5C1e0/m/DJor4IspEQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello,

I have a data set of M features and N observations where I'd like to fit a separate zero-inflated negative binomial model for each feature of the data independently.  In rstan, this would involve adding several loops to fit M rows of data, with a normal distribution for example:

data {
    int M;
    int N[M];
    real y[M,N];
  }
  parameters {
    real mu[M];
  }
  model {
    for (m in 1:M)
      y[m] ~ normal(mu[m], 1);
  }

Is there a way to specify something equivalent to this in a call to brm to avoid compiling for every fit?

Thanks,

Steven

From u6e3dd74b422c061b at groups.google.com  Thu Aug 17 23:33:05 2017
From: u6e3dd74b422c061b at groups.google.com (Paul Buerkner)
Date: Thu, 17 Aug 2017 23:33:05 +0000
Subject: Re: [brms-users] Multiple models in one compilation
Message-ID: <Pxl3QR5C1e0.CITyavciCgAJ@brms-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <Pxl3QR5C1e0.DJor4IspEQAJ@brms-users.groups.google.com>
References: <Pxl3QR5C1e0.DJor4IspEQAJ@brms-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/brms-users/c/Pxl3QR5C1e0/m/CITyavciCgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This is not possible in brms, but you may use the update method to fit these models one after the other without recompiling each of them.

